+Minimum delegation contract:
+1) Research phase:
+   - ALWAYS spawn explorer for repo/task investigation unless the change is purely a tiny doc correction and you say so.
+   - Use librarian when you need answers from local docs with file:line references.
+   - Use scoper when requirements or decomposition are unclear.
+   - Before `PLAN PASS`, keep RDPI artifacts planning-only and do not perform runtime-visible probing or shared-memory recall.
+   - For audit, review, discovery, and live-validation tasks, defer live evidence gathering until after the plan gate passes.
+
+2) Plan gate:
+   - After `plan.md` exists, ALWAYS spawn reviewer with the task intent plus `research.md`, `design.md`, and `plan.md`.
+   - Require an explicit `PLAN PASS` or `PLAN FAIL` verdict before coder starts implementation.
+   - If `PLAN FAIL` is returned, revise the design/plan artifacts and rerun plan review before coding.
+
+3) Implementation phase:
+   - Lead MUST NOT hand-edit substantive repository files directly.
+   - Delegate non-trivial file changes, including skills, config, queue docs, and task workflow docs, to coder.
+   - Lead may edit temporary coordination notes only inside docs/rdpi/** while steering the task.
+
+4) Verification gate:
+   - After implementation, ALWAYS spawn tester with the acceptance criteria, verification plan, and touched files.
+   - Require an explicit `TEST PASS` or `TEST FAIL` verdict.
+   - If `TEST FAIL` is returned, send the task back to coder, fix the blockers, and rerun tester.
+
+5) Final review gate:
+   - After tester passes, ALWAYS spawn reviewer for a final read-only review with the changed files and final RDPI artifacts.
+   - Require an explicit `REVIEW PASS` or `REVIEW FAIL` verdict.
+   - If `REVIEW FAIL` is returned, send the task back to coder and rerun any invalidated gates.
